# 11. Known Historical Issues

The README documents several previously identified issues. Verify that the fixes are complete:

1. HTTP multipart parser discarded bytes after a boundary.
2. Browser-based architecture exposed a localhost API.
3. Passphrase existed in JavaScript/GC-managed memory.
4. Truncation of v1 `.hcx` could be accepted.
5. ML-KEM ciphertext used the wrong encoded type.
6. `mlock()` was incorrectly applied to unaligned memory.
7. plaintext temporarily existed in ordinary `Vec`s.
8. Argon2 memory was previously not locked/zeroized.
9. `mlockall(MCL_FUTURE)` could cause allocation failures.
10. `panic = "abort"` prevented Drop-based zeroization.
11. native file dialogs generated persistent file-name traces.
12. egui TextEdit could retain passphrase copies.
13. secrets/operations in argv would have been visible via `ps`.
14. output files could previously be overwritten.

These are important because they demonstrate that the project has already had several security-relevant implementation defects.

